MT6797 hardware initialization import
===================================

These files come from the verified X20-96 Preloader working tree under
mainline/preloader (donor Git base fa68e7af582c3187182c6825364ceaeacaca2399).
IMPORTS.json records each imported file's original path and content hash.
The original notices remain in each file. Generated GPIO and EMI headers
are frozen inputs for this board, so building SPL does not require the
Preloader build, DCT/emigen tools, or any binary Preloader library.

Only the hardware initialization subset is retained. U-Boot supplies the
entry, C runtime, driver model, MMC command/data transport, GPT parsing,
image loading, console and SPL framework. hardware.c provides board glue,
read-only eFuse access and the few interface functions needed by this
subset. The eFuse address table matches MT6797's 36 devinfo words in the
verified Preloader; it does not call SecLib or SecPlat.

Two imported files have intentional local changes:

* core/inc/print.h: compile print/dbg_print calls away, including their
  format strings and argument evaluation. DRAM training traces are not
  present in the normal SPL binary. spl.c emits only stage results and
  errors, and platform_assert retains the failure file and line.
* drivers/pmic_wrap_init.c: return the final PWRAP retry result, allowing
  SPL to report and stop on initialization failure.

The DRAM algorithms and linked 140-byte EMI record are retained unchanged
from the verified board source. Picachu calibration, security/image-auth
libraries, USB download policy and the original Preloader main/loading
code are not part of this build. This is the unsecured X20 development
board profile; it does not implement image authentication for locked units.

The Makefile isolates the legacy types/features from U-Boot headers and
keeps r8 (donor ABI) and r9 (U-Boot gd) reserved. Timer and UART helper
symbols are namespaced to avoid replacing U-Boot's implementations.

Use mainline/x20-sbc/tools/build-x20-spl.sh from the workspace. The script
checks the linked EMI bytes, SRAM/DT layout, BootROM GFH SHA, absent binary
libraries and absent training strings. Runtime evidence and rollback are
in docs/UBOOT-SPL-20261030.md at the workspace root.
